# 💬 AI Chat Composer & Panel UI Patterns (Helix Standard)

## 🎯 The Horizontal Cramping Problem
In AI-assisted canvas editors, CAD tools, and studio side-panels (typically 320px–420px wide), placing action buttons on the left and a verbose rectangular send button (e.g., "Надіслати" / "Send", 90–110px wide) on the right squashes the central `<textarea>` to ~200px or less. This causes multiline text to warp aggressively and frustrates users.

## 📐 Canonical Solution: Unified Prompt Composer (Helix Dark Teal)

### 1. Structural Layout
Replace 3-column flex rows with a **Unified Composer Card**:
```tsx
<div className="chat-input-box">
  {/* Mention popup anchored to the top of the composer card */}
  {mentionsOpen && <MentionMenu />}

  {/* Full-width text area (zero lateral competition) */}
  <textarea
    className="chat-textarea"
    rows={2}
    placeholder="Ask AI or type instructions (@ for cards)..."
  />

  {/* Action toolbar inside the card footer */}
  <div className="chat-box-footer">
    <div className="chat-actions">
      <button type="button" className="chat-action-btn attach-btn" title="Attach file">+</button>
      <button type="button" className="chat-action-btn tpl-btn" title="Pick template">◫</button>
    </div>
    <button
      type="button"
      className="chat-round-send-btn"
      title="Send"
      disabled={!input.trim()}
    >
      {busy ? <span className="btn-spinner" /> : <UpArrowIcon />}
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
```

### 2. Design Tokens & Styling Invariants
- **Textarea Width**: `width: 100% !important;` borderless, background transparent, padding 0.
- **Round Send Button**:
  * Dimensions: `32px` width, `32px` height, `border-radius: 50%`.
  * Background: Helix Teal `--accent: #35d5d5`, hover `--accent-hover: #22c55e`.
  * Icon: 15×15px SVG up-arrow (`↑`), dark `#0b0f10`.
  * Spinner: 13×13px centered circular spinner when `busy === true`.
- **Action Buttons**:
  * Compact `28px × 28px` rounded rectangles (`border-radius: 8px`).
  * Subtle translucent background (`rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04)`), highlighting on hover.

### 3. Defensive Serialization (`omitData`)
When serializing canvas card state for LLM context, guard against undefined background or asset values:
```ts
function sanitizeCardData(card: CanvasCard) {
  const bg = typeof card.background === "string" ? card.background : "";
  const isBase64 = bg.startsWith("data:image");
  return {
    ...card,
    background: isBase64 ? "[IMAGE_BASE64_OMITTED]" : bg,
  };
}
```
